Changes made to the original
----------------------------

This is an adaptation, and ShareAlike applies to it. What was changed:

  * Only 18 of the development split's 20 databases are drawn from, so the questions on the
    other two are not represented at all. wta_1 (about 105 MB) was excluded by a 5 MB size
    limit; museum_visit is not in the source pool this slice was built from.
  * A 300-row subset of the development split was selected (seed 42), not the whole set.
  * Rows whose gold query returns an empty result set were removed.
  * Rows whose question paraphrases one already kept were removed -- 2 of them, by three-word
    shingles and Jaccard similarity at 0.7.
  * Each row was labelled with a difficulty band, computed with Spider's own official
    hardness classifier, and assigned to a tuning or holdout split.
  * Rows were reshaped into one flat JSON object per line.
  * Only the SQLite databases these 300 questions need are included, not Spider's full
    166-database set.

spider/build_slice.py in the source repository reproduces all of it.

What ShareAlike means here
--------------------------

ShareAlike attaches to Adapted Material -- these rows or these databases modified, transformed
or built upon -- and it applies when you share that material. Share an adaptation and it goes
out under CC BY-SA 4.0 with the attribution above. It does not reach everything a run
produces: model outputs, scores and reports are not the data.

That obligation travels with the data, not with the code, and it does not go away if the data
is copied somewhere else. Publishing this repository, or a generated project containing these
rows, is a redistribution: this file must travel with it.
